@gatewayBaseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Scenario 33
### Attachment metadata is coordinated through storage-service + MinIO-outside-XA saga

### 33.1 Login as landlord
# @name loginLandlord
POST {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1
}

### 33.2 Initialize attachment metadata
# @name initAttachment
POST {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/attachments/init
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLandlord.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "originalFilename": "sofa-damage.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg"
}

### 33.3 Confirm object upload
### Demo note: STORAGE_VERIFY_MINIO_OBJECT=false by default, so this confirms metadata after an out-of-band MinIO upload.
# @name confirmAttachment
POST {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/attachments/{{initAttachment.response.body.$.id}}/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLandlord.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "objectKey": "{{initAttachment.response.body.$.objectKey}}"
}

### 33.4 Create claim with attachment ref; claim-service emits ATTACHMENT_BINDING_REQUESTED
# @name createClaim
POST {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/claims
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLandlord.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "tenantUserId": 3,
  "title": "Damage claim with attachment",
  "description": "Attachment binding is handled by storage-service through Kafka.",
  "claimedAmount": 80.00,
  "currency": "USD",
  "attachmentIds": [{{initAttachment.response.body.$.id}}]
}

### 33.5 Poll claim attachments until status becomes BOUND
GET {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/claims/{{createClaim.response.body.$.id}}/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLandlord.response.body.$.token}}

### 33.6 Inspect storage metadata
GET {{gatewayBaseUrl}}/api/attachments/{{initAttachment.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLandlord.response.body.$.token}}
